        <h2>Platform-Specific Tips</h2>

        <h3>WordPress</h3>
        <p>WordPress generates multiple sizes by default, but you should still optimize the originals. Use a plugin like ShortPixel or Smush for automatic compression. Enable WebP serving through your CDN or a plugin.</p>

        <h3>Shopify</h3>
        <p>Shopify automatically compresses and serves WebP images through its CDN. However, you should still upload reasonably sized originals — don't upload 10MB files and expect Shopify to handle it gracefully.</p>

        <h3>Static Sites (Hugo, Astro, Next.js)</h3>
        <p>Pre-compress images at build time. Use build plugins or scripts to automatically convert images to WebP and generate responsive sizes. Serve images through a CDN for global performance.</p>

